cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Global Building Explorer"
abstract: >-
  A single-file web application that streams building footprints, heights and
  historical satellite imagery for anywhere on Earth. Each building can be queried for
  its measured footprint geometry, its exact count of physically touching neighbours,
  and estimated height, storeys and population share. A selected area additionally
  yields density, footprint distribution, coverage measured from the union of
  rasterised footprints, and block complexity — the street-access metric for informal
  settlement — exported as a georeferenced two-colour instance mask with its statistics
  and provenance. Users may load their own imagery or polygons and have them scored
  against the published data. All computation is client-side; no data is stored or
  uploaded. Built as the delivered product of a study on segmenting individual
  buildings in dense informal settlements.
type: software
